meta {
  name: manage organisations
  type: http
  seq: 15
}

post {
  url: {{SUPABASE_URL}}/rest/v1/rpc/organisations
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  apikey: {{SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY}}
  Authorization: Bearer {{SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept-Profile: {{SUPABASE_API_SCHEMA}}
  Content-Profile: {{SUPABASE_API_SCHEMA}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "input_payload": {
      "action": "list",
      "handle": "example-organisation"
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Authenticated organisation management boundary. The RPC derives user and session identity from the verified JWT; clients must never supply either identifier. Anonymous users cannot execute it.

  Read and context actions:
  - "list"
  - "create" with name, handle, and optional colourHex
  - "switch" with handle
  - "read" with handle or organisationId
  - "handle.available" with handle; returns false for existing, invalid, or reserved handles

  Manager actions:
  - "update" with handle or organisationId plus any of name, handle, bio, colourHex, avatarPath, headerImagePath, or accessPolicy ("closed" or "request")
  - "members.list"
  - "members.add" with userId and role
  - "members.updateRole" with userId and role
  - "members.remove" with userId
  - "invites.list"
  - "invites.create" with email and role; the raw inviteToken is returned once and only its SHA-256 hash is stored
  - "invites.revoke" with invitationId
  - "access.list", "access.approve", or "access.reject" with requestId

  Account actions:
  - "invites.accept" with token; the signed-in Auth email must equal the normalised invitation email and the token must be unexpired, unrevoked, and unused
  - "access.request" with handle; allowed only when that organisation's accessPolicy is "request"

  Canonical roles are "owner", "admin", and "member". The last owner cannot be removed or demoted. Creation, switching, invitation acceptance, handle changes, and role changes return requiresSessionRefresh when the browser must refresh its Supabase session before relying on organisation JWT claims.
}
